addresses.comment:
**The shared entry for putting rebel or partisan brigades in a province**, five call sites: SpawnRebelsTextCommand (0x43DF5A), SpawnRebelsOfChosenTypeInProvince (0x4C114E), SpawnPartisansFromUnderground (0x50B92B, the only caller passing forActor = true, with the exile's tag), CCreateRebelsEffect::Execute and CCreateRevoltEffect::Execute. 0x4C1160 to the two `ret 0x10` at 0x4C1360 and 0x4C142C. Read whole on the listing:

    if (!province->area->slot0() || !province->path_node->simulated (+0x13D)) return
    if (count < 1) count = 1
    if (forActor) faction = the first of +0xC7C with type == rebelType and country.id (+0x3C) == actor->id
    else          faction = FindRebelFactionForProvince(province, rebelType)
    SetProvinceRevoltRisk(province, 0, false)                 ; before the null test
    if (faction) {
        if (province->controller != REB) RebelFaction_AddTarget(faction, controller tag, id)
        CreateRebelsForFaction(actor, faction, &tmp, province, count, forActor)
    } else
        CreateRebelFaction(rebelType, province, state, count, "", forActor, actor)

So **revolt risk is zeroed whenever the two gates pass**, also when no faction can be found or made - a null rebelType (every type scoring 0 in ChooseRebelTypeForProvince) zeroes it and makes nothing. There is no log on that path; the string pushed at 0x4C137F is the empty string at 0x15B4945, the new faction's name argument, which the constructor never reads. Signature corrected 2026-10-02 by the signature audit (reversing/findings/FINDINGS-sigaudit.md); parameter names 2026-10-14.
